A||N||10||TRL46202||Has anyone ever.......||||1||
Z||000000||TRL46202||03-10-2000||01:54 AM||||Question, has anyone ever removed the material that is attached to the engine bay walls? Mine was in such bad shape, Oil,dirt,torn just plain nasty that I took it off or should I say fell off. Do I need to replace it. I thought about just painting the engine bay and leaving it that way. Any thoughts.....||||reg||1
Z||000001||FIEROCIOUS||03-10-2000||02:02 AM||||That was the first thing I did to my Fiero! It is a sound deadening and heat insulator. Take all of it off except for the firewall, the wall directly behind your seat. The benifits are less heat in engine compartment, it looks beter, make the car sound meaner, and less posibility of rust. (It soaks up water and holds it) This is just MY opinion!||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||03-10-2000||12:16 PM||||Did the same on my V6 and my wife's 4 cyl. The results on the 4 were even more impressive because you obviously can see more of the walls. But in both I kept the cabin firewall covered since they weren't too bad. No more fiberglass on the underside of my arms! Woohoo!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||87SC/GT||03-10-2000||01:00 PM||||BRM racing sells a replacement insulation that is good to 1200 degrees and will not hold moisture. It was developed by NASA . Here's the problem, It's about 200.00 a square foot!||||reg||7
Z||000004||Spyder||03-10-2000||01:19 PM||||I removed mine when it started falling into the belts.  I bought some of the engine insulation with the aluminum backing and decided once I removed all of the old, I really didn’t need it. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spyder||03-10-2000||01:23 PM||||Also, semi gloss black paint  matches the original very well.  I used the spray paint that was under a dollar a can and it looks great and clean.||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||03-10-2000||05:25 PM||||I ripped mine out recently and it made the bay look much cleaner.  Just don't inhale all the crap that flies around when you yank it out.  Nasty...||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||03-10-2000||06:09 PM||||thats something that i have been questioning too.  does jc whitney sell anything like this?<P>as for the sound deadning, you can pull back you carpet and apply dynamat to the inside fo the car.  this will give you great "sound deadning' qualities.  also, at one time, they use to make a insert for firewalls and hoods of other vehicles.  <P>might be worth checking into!?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||03-10-2000||06:48 PM||||On the sides it's only noise killer. Rip it out if you want too.<P>Definatly wear a decent partical mask when ripping it out. The insulation is fiberglass, but because the brakes are near by there may be some amount of asbestose in it in addition to dir oil etc. If you use a disposable mask make sure it's tight to your face. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gokart||03-10-2000||07:52 PM||||That's all I needed to hear! I'll be removing mine tomorrow since it's falling apart anyway!||||reg||14
